  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the minimum batch size for training, presenting a binary choice that constitutes one independent query."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The 50 new workers must be trained \"by the end of the 8th week\" — does this mean all 50 must have completed their 2-week training (i.e., be fully productive) by the end of week 8, or does it mean all 50 must have started training by the end of week 8 (some could still be in training at the end of week 8)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the definition of the training deadline (completion vs. start), which constitutes one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "does this mean that if demand in a given week is not fully met, the unmet amount incurs a penalty of 0.5 yuan/kg (for food I) or 0.6 yuan/kg (for food II) for that week, and the unmet demand is simply lost (not carried over to the next week)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for confirmation of a single specific interpretation regarding the penalty calculation and the treatment of unmet demand (lost vs. carried over). Although it contains two clauses, they are linked by 'and' to define one specific scenario/policy choice, so a user answers the entire premise with a single yes/no or correction."
}

